#N canvas 20 20 1450 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 u_err -- the error bus. Anything reports with [s err] and a message box: <level> <source> <text> \, where level is info \, warn or fail (C-12). This decides what reaches the screen \; g_oled decides how it looks. ref/module/error.md, f 58;
#X text 20 120 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X declare -path ../mac-stubs;
#X text 20 170 U_ERR DOES NOT DRAW. C-5 allows exactly one abstraction to send on oscOut \, and that is g_oled \, so this forwards onto disp as alert <level> <source> <text> instead. plan-v04.md says u_err draws to the ALERT buffer \; where the two disagree the convention wins -- two writers \, one screen., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r err;
#X obj 20 340 t a a a;
#X obj 20 400 route warn fail info;
#X obj 110 445 r \$0-verbose;
#X obj 20 490 spigot;
#X obj 20 530 list prepend alert warn;
#X obj 20 570 list trim;
#X obj 20 610 s disp;
#X obj 700 470 list prepend alert fail;
#X obj 700 510 list trim;
#X obj 700 550 s disp;
#X obj 1050 470 print err-BAD-LEVEL;
#X obj 1050 390 print err;
#X obj 560 230 loadbang;
#X obj 700 180 r mode;
#X obj 700 220 route compose perform;
#X msg 700 270 1;
#X msg 800 270 0;
#X obj 700 320 s \$0-verbose;
#X text 20 700 The bus is unfiltered \, only the screen is: the print fires on every error whatever the mode., f 46;
#X text 20 820 route \, not select: mode arrives as a bare selector \, which select has no method for., f 46;
#X text 20 940 Three levels. info is logged and never drawn \, so its outlet goes nowhere \, while the log tap above this route sees every level. A level that is none of the three falls out of the reject and is printed rather than swallowed (C-12)., f 46;
#X text 480 700 Defaults to verbose \, the state before any mode arrives: seeing every warning is the useful default \, and the worst case is an error you did not need., f 46;
#X text 480 820 Error text is one line of 21 characters: gPrintln does not wrap \, so only the call site can shorten it. C-12, f 46;
#X text 480 940 Callers use a message box \, which carries the level as its selector. C-6, f 46;
#N canvas 30 30 1700 1750 logfile 0;
#X text 20 20 The log that survives the session. Capture is unconditional: the menu-launched patch has no console to scroll back., f 58;
#X text 20 145 Two files: text write rewrites the whole file \, so this holds only the session \, cut-it-err.cur \, and logroll.sh carries it into cut-it-err.log at load with a wall-clock stamp. tools/fetch-errors.sh reads both (ref/module/error.md)., f 58;
